<title>SiliCool</title>
<meta name="description" content="Fan Control. For Apple silicon. Every sensor your Mac reports, in your menu bar — and the fans macOS never gives you a way to touch.">
<style>
/* ── SiliCool ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Light paper, dark product panels, system type. The app's own screenshots
   are dark, so they sit on the page as objects rather than blending into it.
   No webfonts: SF Pro is already on every Mac this ships to.              */
:root {
  --paper: #fbfdff;
  --tint: #eef3f8;
  --tint-deep: #dde7f1;
  --ink: #071727;
  --muted: #5a6b7c;
  --faint: #8d9aa8;
  --line: #dfe7ef;
  --accent: #0a6cff;
  --panel: #0b1017;
  --panel-line: #1d242e;
  --panel-ink: #eef2f7;
  --panel-muted: #8e99a6;
  --panel-accent: #4da3ff;
  --ember: #ff8a3d;
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
html { scroll-behavior: smooth; -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }
body {
  margin: 0; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink);
  font-family: -apple-system, system-ui, "SF Pro Display", "SF Pro Text", "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
  font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.6; -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}
img, video { display: block; max-width: 100%; }
a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
h1, h2, h3 { margin: 0; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.021em; text-wrap: balance; }
h1 { font-size: clamp(42px, 6.6vw, 76px); line-height: 1.025; }
h2 { font-size: clamp(31px, 4.2vw, 53px); line-height: 1.04; }
h3 { font-size: clamp(21px, 2.4vw, 30px); line-height: 1.12; }
p { margin: 0; }
.mono { font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; }
.wrap { width: min(1120px, 100% - 48px); margin-inline: auto; }
.narrow { max-width: 640px; }
.lede { font-size: clamp(18px, 1.9vw, 21px); color: var(--muted); letter-spacing: -0.011em; }
.eyebrow {
  font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: var(--accent);
  margin-bottom: 18px;
}

/* ── nav ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
header.nav {
  position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 60;
  background: rgba(251, 253, 255, 0);
  transition: background .25s ease, border-color .25s ease;
  border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
}
header.nav.stuck {
  background: rgba(251, 253, 255, .82);
  backdrop-filter: saturate(180%) blur(18px);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: saturate(180%) blur(18px);
  border-bottom-color: var(--line);
}
header.nav .row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; padding: 14px 0; }
header.nav img { width: 30px; height: 30px; border-radius: 8px; }
header.nav .brand { font-weight: 700; font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
header.nav .right { margin-left: auto; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 20px; }
header.nav .right a.text { font-size: 15px; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 500; }
header.nav .right a.text:hover { color: var(--ink); }
@media (max-width: 640px) { header.nav .right a.text { display: none; } }

/* ── buttons ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.btn {
  display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 9px;
  border-radius: 999px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  font-family: inherit; cursor: pointer; border: 1px solid transparent;
  transition: background .2s ease, color .2s ease, border-color .2s ease, transform .2s ease;
}
.btn.primary { background: var(--ink); color: #fff; }
.btn.primary:hover { background: #14283c; transform: translateY(-1px); }
.btn.ghost { background: transparent; color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--line); }
.btn.ghost:hover { border-color: var(--faint); transform: translateY(-1px); }
.btn.sm { font-size: 15px; padding: 9px 18px; }
.btn.lg { font-size: 21px; padding: 15px 30px; }
.btn.on-dark.ghost { color: var(--panel-ink); border-color: var(--panel-line); }
.btn.on-dark.ghost:hover { border-color: var(--panel-muted); }
:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 3px; border-radius: 6px; }

/* ── scroll reveal ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Applied only once JS confirms it can undo it, so the page still reads with
   scripting off and the first frame is never a blank screen.               */
.js .reveal { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(22px); }
.js .reveal.shown {
  opacity: 1; transform: none;
  transition: opacity .7s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1), transform .7s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1);
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  html { scroll-behavior: auto; }
  .js .reveal { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  .btn:hover { transform: none; }
}

/* ── hero ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.hero { padding: clamp(56px, 9vw, 116px) 0 clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px); }
.hero { text-align: center; }
.hero h1, .hero .lede { margin-inline: auto; }
.hero h1 { max-width: 15ch; }
.hero .lede { margin-top: 24px; max-width: 46ch; }
.hero .actions { display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 38px; }
.hero .req { margin-top: 20px; font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--faint); letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
.hero .req b { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; }

.showcase {
  margin-top: clamp(40px, 5vw, 70px);
  background: var(--panel); border-radius: 26px; padding: clamp(14px, 1.6vw, 22px);
  box-shadow: 0 30px 70px rgba(7, 23, 39, .16), 0 2px 8px rgba(7, 23, 39, .06);
}
.showcase video { border-radius: 14px; width: 100%; }

/* ── keyword rail ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.rail {
  display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px 12px; justify-content: center;
  padding: clamp(44px, 6vw, 76px) 0;
}
.rail span {
  font-size: 15px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.015em; color: var(--muted);
  background: var(--tint); border-radius: 999px; padding: 8px 16px;
}

/* ── sections ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
section { padding: clamp(56px, 8vw, 112px) 0; }
section.tinted { background: var(--tint); }
.head { max-width: 22ch; }
.head + .lede { margin-top: 20px; max-width: 56ch; }

/* dark inset panel */
.panel {
  background: var(--panel); color: var(--panel-ink);
  border-radius: 28px; padding: clamp(30px, 4.6vw, 68px);
}
.panel h2, .panel h3 { color: var(--panel-ink); }
.panel .lede, .panel p { color: var(--panel-muted); }
.panel .eyebrow { color: var(--panel-accent); }

.trio { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr)); gap: clamp(24px, 3vw, 40px); margin-top: 48px; }
.trio img { border-radius: 14px; width: 100%; border: 1px solid var(--panel-line); }
.trio h3 { font-size: 20px; margin-top: 22px; letter-spacing: -0.018em; }
.trio p { font-size: 15.5px; margin-top: 8px; }

/* ── data table ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.scroller { overflow-x: auto; margin-top: 44px; }
table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 16px; min-width: 620px; }
th {
  text-align: left; font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .02em;
  text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--faint); padding: 0 16px 12px 0;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
}
td { padding: 16px 16px 16px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: baseline; }
td.v { font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace; font-size: 15px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
td.why { color: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; }
.panel table, .panel th, .panel td { border-color: var(--panel-line); }
.panel th { color: var(--panel-muted); }
.panel td.why { color: var(--panel-muted); }
code {
  font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace; font-size: .88em;
  background: var(--tint-deep); padding: 2px 7px; border-radius: 6px;
}
.panel code { background: #182029; color: var(--panel-ink); }

/* ── steps ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr)); gap: clamp(26px, 3vw, 44px); margin-top: 52px; }
.step .n {
  width: 32px; height: 32px; border-radius: 999px; display: grid; place-items: center;
  background: var(--ink); color: #fff; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 18px;
}
.step h3 { font-size: 20px; letter-spacing: -0.018em; }
.step p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 15.5px; margin-top: 8px; }
.dmg-shot { margin-top: 52px; border-radius: 20px; overflow: hidden; box-shadow: 0 24px 60px rgba(7,23,39,.14); }

/* ── statement ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.statement { padding: clamp(70px, 10vw, 130px) 0; text-align: center; }
.statement h2 { max-width: 18ch; margin-inline: auto; }
.statement p { margin: 24px auto 0; max-width: 56ch; }

/* ── faq ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.faq { margin-top: 44px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
details { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
summary {
  cursor: pointer; list-style: none; padding: 22px 0; font-weight: 600; font-size: 18px;
  letter-spacing: -0.018em; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 16px;
}
summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
summary::after {
  content: ""; margin-left: auto; width: 11px; height: 11px; flex: none;
  border-right: 2px solid var(--faint); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--faint);
  transform: rotate(45deg) translate(-3px, -3px); transition: transform .25s ease;
}
details[open] summary::after { transform: rotate(-135deg) translate(-3px, -3px); }
details p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 16px; padding-bottom: 26px; max-width: 62ch; }

/* ── footer ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
.close { text-align: center; padding: clamp(64px, 9vw, 120px) 0; }
.close .actions { display: flex; gap: 14px; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 36px; }
footer { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 30px 0 56px; }
footer .row { display: flex; gap: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--faint); }
footer a { color: var(--muted); }
footer a:hover { color: var(--ink); }
</style>

<header class="nav" id="nav">
  <div class="wrap row">
    <img src="assets/icon.png" alt="">
    <span class="brand">SiliCool</span>
    <div class="right">
      <a class="text" href="#reads">What it reads</a>
      <a class="text" href="#install">Install</a>
      <a class="text" href="#faq">FAQ</a>
      <a class="btn primary sm" id="nav-download" href="#"> Download</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="wrap hero">
  <h1>Fan Control.<br/> For  silicon.</h1>
  <p class="lede">Every sensor your Mac reports, in your menu bar <br/> and the fans macOS never gives you a way to touch.</p>
  <div class="actions">
    <a class="btn primary lg" id="download-button" href="#"> Download for Mac</a>
    <a class="btn ghost lg" href="#reads">See what it reads</a>
  </div>
  <p class="req" id="download-meta"><b>3.3 MB</b> · version 1.0 · macOS 14 or later · Apple silicon · free and MIT licensed</p>

  <div class="showcase">
    <video src="assets/promo.mp4" poster="assets/poster.jpg" autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="metadata"></video>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="wrap rail reveal">
  <span>256 live sensors</span>
  <span>Two fans, held where you want</span>
  <span>Fan curves</span>
  <span>10 minutes of history</span>
  <span>Light and dark</span>
  <span>No telemetry, ever</span>
  <span>15 MB resident</span>
</div>

<section id="reads" class="wrap">
  <div class="panel reveal">
    <div class="eyebrow">What it reads</div>
    <h2 class="head">One panel. No window to manage.</h2>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:20px; max-width:52ch;">Click the menu bar and the whole app is there — sensors grouped in a fixed order, ten minutes of history, and the controls underneath.</p>

    <div class="trio">
      <div>
        <img src="assets/panel-monitor.jpg" alt="SiliCool's panel showing the fan gauge, controls and grouped sensors" loading="lazy">
        <h3>Grouped, and still</h3>
        <p>CPU cores, GPU, memory, SoC, storage, battery, enclosure, power. In a fixed order that never re-sorts itself while you are reading it.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <img src="assets/panel-curve.jpg" alt="The fan curve editor with four draggable anchor points" loading="lazy">
        <h3>Curves you draw</h3>
        <p>Four anchors at 50, 65, 80 and 95 °C. Drag them, or start from Quiet, Balanced or Aggressive. A marker shows where you are on the curve right now.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <img src="assets/panel-settings.jpg" alt="SiliCool settings showing menu bar options and machine details" loading="lazy">
        <h3>Follows your Mac</h3>
        <p>Light and dark. Choose what the menu bar shows — rpm, CPU °C, hottest °C, watts, or just the icon.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tinted">
  <div class="wrap reveal">
    <div class="eyebrow">Measured, not claimed</div>
    <h2 class="head">Every number here came off a real machine.</h2>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:20px;">Taken on a MacBook Pro — Mac17,9, M5 Pro, 24 GB. Yours will report its own.</p>

    <div class="scroller">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Reading</th><th>Value</th><th>How</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Fans found</td><td class="v">2 · 2317–7826 rpm</td><td class="why">SMC keys <code>F0Ac</code>, <code>F0Mn</code>, <code>F0Mx</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td>CPU cores</td><td class="v">5 Super · 10 Performance</td><td class="why">from <code>hw.perflevelN</code>, not a lookup table</td></tr>
          <tr><td>GPU cores</td><td class="v">16</td><td class="why">IORegistry <code>gpu-core-count</code> — against 42 GPU probes</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sample cost</td><td class="v">15 ms</td><td class="why">84 keys, on a background task</td></tr>
          <tr><td>First scan</td><td class="v">2.8 s</td><td class="why">enumerate, then three sweeps to find duplicate keys</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Idle footprint</td><td class="v">15 MB</td><td class="why">panel closed; the gauge stops when nobody is looking</td></tr>
          <tr><td>History window</td><td class="v">14,400 bytes</td><td class="why">10 minutes at 1 Hz in a fixed ring buffer</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap statement reveal">
  <h2>Probes are not parts.</h2>
  <p class="lede">Your Mac exposes 42 GPU die sensors and has 16 GPU cores. Nothing published says which sensor sits on which core — so SiliCool only calls something a core when the count matches what the OS reports, and labels the rest as probes rather than inventing hardware you don't have.</p>
</section>

<section id="install" class="tinted">
  <div class="wrap reveal">
    <div class="eyebrow">Install</div>
    <h2 class="head">Drag, open, approve.</h2>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:20px; max-width:58ch;">Sensors work the second you open it. Fan control needs one approval, because writing to the SMC requires root.</p>

    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <div class="n">1</div>
        <h3>Drag it to Applications</h3>
        <p>It has to run from there: macOS ties the approval to where the app lives, and SiliCool will tell you rather than let you approve something that cannot work.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="n">2</div>
        <h3>Allow it once</h3>
        <p>macOS will say it can't verify the developer. Open <strong>System Settings › Privacy &amp; Security</strong>, scroll to Security, and click <strong>Open Anyway</strong>. Once only — after that it opens normally.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="n">3</div>
        <h3>Enable fan control</h3>
        <p>Sensors are already live. For the fans, press Enable Fan Control, then switch SiliCool on under System Settings › General › Login Items &amp; Extensions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top:44px; padding:26px 28px; background:var(--paper); border-radius:18px; border:1px solid var(--line);">
      <h3 style="font-size:19px;">Why does macOS warn about it?</h3>
      <p style="color:var(--muted); font-size:15.5px; margin-top:10px; max-width:62ch;">Because SiliCool isn't notarized yet — Apple's automated malware scan requires a paid developer account, which this project doesn't have. The app <em>is</em> signed, so macOS can still tell you who built it and detect any tampering since. The source is public and MIT licensed if you'd rather read it than trust it.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap">
  <div class="panel reveal">
    <div class="eyebrow">Safety</div>
    <h2 class="head">A pinned fan stays pinned. So every exit hands it back.</h2>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:20px; max-width:52ch;">Fan settings outlive the process that made them. SiliCool treats that as its problem, not yours.</p>

    <div class="scroller">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>When SiliCool stops</th><th>What happens to your fans</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Your Mac goes to sleep</td><td class="why">returned to automatic, then picked back up on wake</td></tr>
          <tr><td>You quit it, or log out</td><td class="why">returned to automatic</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Ctrl-C in a terminal</td><td class="why">returned to automatic</td></tr>
          <tr><td><code>kill</code>, or a system shutdown</td><td class="why">returned to automatic</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Force Quit, <code>kill -9</code></td><td class="why">not trappable by any app — see below</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap statement reveal">
  <h2>SiliCool can't survive a Force Quit.</h2>
  <p class="lede">No app can — <code>SIGKILL</code> cannot be caught by the process it kills. If you force quit SiliCool while a fan is held, it stays held: nothing is left running to hand it back. Reopen SiliCool and press Release, or restart. Every other way of stopping the app — quitting, logging out, sleeping, <code>Ctrl-C</code> — gives the fans back first.</p>
</section>

<section id="faq" class="tinted">
  <div class="wrap reveal narrow" style="max-width:820px;">
    <div class="eyebrow">Questions</div>
    <h2 class="head">Worth asking before installing a fan controller.</h2>

    <div class="faq">
      <details open>
        <summary>Can this damage my Mac?</summary>
        <p>SiliCool can only ask for speeds between the minimum and maximum the fan itself reports — 2317 and 7826 rpm on this machine. It cannot stop a fan the system wants running, and it cannot exceed the hardware's own ceiling. Thermal throttling is handled by your Mac's firmware and keeps working regardless. Running fans faster is the safe direction.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>macOS says it can't verify the developer. Is that a problem?</summary>
        <p>It means SiliCool hasn't been through Apple's notarization service, which requires a paid Apple Developer account. It does <em>not</em> mean the app is unsigned or altered — it carries a valid Apple-issued signature, so macOS can identify the developer and will refuse to launch it if a single byte has been changed since it was built. To open it: System Settings › Privacy &amp; Security › Open Anyway. If that makes you uncomfortable, don't install it — read the source and build it yourself instead.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does it collect any data?</summary>
        <p>No. No analytics, no telemetry, no accounts, and no networking code at all — readings have no way to leave your Mac. See the <a href="privacy.html" style="color:var(--accent)">privacy page</a>.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Why does it need an admin approval?</summary>
        <p>Writing fan keys to the SMC requires root. Rather than running the whole app as root, SiliCool installs a small launchd daemon that does nothing but four privileged calls, and talks to it over XPC. Both ends verify each other's code signature, so nothing else on your Mac can drive your fans through it. Remove it from Settings at any time.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does it work on Intel Macs?</summary>
        <p>Not yet. The sensor naming, the core-count checks and the manual-mode key all target Apple silicon. Intel Macs use different SMC keys for the same things, and would need their own testing before it would be trustworthy.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What happens if I delete the app?</summary>
        <p>Use <strong>Remove helper</strong> in Settings first — it returns the fans to automatic and unregisters the daemon. Deleting the app removes both, since the daemon lives inside the bundle, but the fans should be handed back before that happens.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="wrap close reveal">
  <h2>Completely open-source</h2>
  <p class="lede" style="margin:22px auto 0; max-width:44ch;">No account, no subscription. <br/> Just the numbers your Mac already knows.</p>
